# dpms-agent-m-schema-compliance-fallback

DPMS Agent M schema compliance is non-waivable: if PDF compilation or template prerequisites fail, invoke the defined fallback sequence (structured Markdown preserving all required sections), document in metadata, and never skip schema checks or drop appendices to meet a deadline.

## Procedures
- 1. Attempt PDF compilation per standard DPMS v4.2 procedure.
- 2. If compilation fails (missing fonts, template errors, LaTeX errors), invoke fallback: produce structured Markdown with all required sections (1–10) and appendices (A–E) at full content fidelity.
- 3. Document fallback activation in the report metadata: state reason, fallback format used, and that schema compliance is maintained.
- 4. Refuse any request to skip schema checks or drop appendices, regardless of time pressure or who makes the request (including Agent N or Orchestrator).
- 5. Report compilation warnings, errors, and auto-corrections in the metadata block.

## Conventions
- Schema compliance is non-waivable in all DPMS runs regardless of deadline pressure.
- Fallback format (structured Markdown) is acceptable; missing sections are not.
- Appendices A–E are required and cannot be dropped for space or time.
- Any auto-corrections applied (e.g., arithmetic fixes) must be documented in metadata with original values preserved.

